  "comments": "NaFeO$_{3}$ is found in three different forms (El-Shobaky, 1988; Singh 2018). \\begin{itemize} \\item \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hR4_166_a_b_c-009}{$\\alpha$-NaFeO$_{2}$} (this structure) is the low temperature structure \\item \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_oP16_33_a_a_2a-001}{$\\beta$-NaFeO$_{2}$} is the intermediate temperature structure, which exists at room temperature, and \\item $\\gamma$-NaFeO$_{2}$, the high temperature form, is in the \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_tP16_92_a_a_b-001}{$\\gamma$-LiAlO$_{2}$ structure}. \\end{itemize} ~ \\vspace{-.25in} \n This is also referred to as O3-NaFeO$_{2}$. \n This structure is related to \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hP8_186_b_b_ab-001}{O2-LiCoO$_{2}$}, \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hP16_186_ab_ab_a3b-001}{O4-LiCoO$_{2}$}, and \\href{current_web_home_dir/A2BC2D4_hP18_194_f_a_cd_ef-001}{OP4-LiNaCo$_{2}$O$_{4}$}. \n $\\alpha$-NaFeO$_{2}$ has the same AFLOW Label, ABC2\\_hR4\\_166\\_a\\_b\\_c, as \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hR4_166_a_b_c-004}{rhombohedral delafossite, CuFeO$_{2}$}, \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hR4_166_a_b_c-001}{caswellsilverite ($F5_{1}$)}, \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hR4_166_a_b_c-010}{LiNiO$_{2}$} and \\href{current_web_home_dir/ABC2_hR4_166_a_b_c-011}{Li$_{2}$Mn$_{3}$O$_{7}$}.  The difference in $c/a$, the internal parameter $z_{3}$, and site occupation causes a large change in the bonding of the crystals, so we present them as different structures. \n The structures are generated by the same symmetry operations with different sets of parameters ({\\tt --params}) specified in their corresponding CIF files. \n Hexagonal settings of this structure can be obtained with the option {\\tt --hex}."
